  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2025 IFRC MENA health evacuations from Gaza</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A humanitarian health intervention led by the IFRC, worth &#x20ac;4.32 million, to support medical evacuations and recovery for Palestinians from Gaza through treatment, rehabilitation, and psychosocial care.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Because Gaza&#x2019;s health system has collapsed after months of conflict. Thousands of civilians, particularly children, suffer from severe injuries, chronic illnesses, disabilities, and trauma, while local hospitals are unable to provide care.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">By providing specialized hospital care, surgery, rehabilitation, psychosocial support, basic assistance, and family reunification services. In Egypt, ERCS also manages humanitarian logistics, processing thousands of aid trucks and ambulances into Gaza. The operation combines direct service delivery, coordination with ministries, and donor support to ensure sustained, dignified care for evacuees and host communities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">It targets around 3,500 people: 500 evacuees and caregivers in Jordan and 3,000 in Egypt (including discharged patients and people in rehabilitation). Beneficiaries include war-wounded children, chronically ill patients, and their families.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The operation covers Jordan and Egypt, implemented by the Jordan National Red Crescent Society (JNRCS) and the Egyptian Red Crescent Society (ERCS) under the IFRC Middle East Crisis Emergency Appeal (2025&#x2013;2026).</narrative>
  </description>
